Author: Nick Hung <nick@andestech.com>
Date:   Sat Jun 13 05:52:38 2026 +0800

    behavioral: privilege round-trips across the handoff (L6 resolved)

    The plugin drains the gdbstub priv virtual register instead of
    hardcoding M; vsim's ResumeDriver writes dcsr.prv before dret (verified
    read-back: an M-only RTL like the default ax45mpv_premium WARL-pins the
    field and the resume aborts with a pick-an-S/U-capable-engine error)
    and mirrors the producer's PMP block for S/U states (without it an S/U
    ROI cannot fetch on a PMP-implementing core -- L2 partial); StateDrain
    reads dcsr.prv back at the exit halt.

    e2e: rt_priv_smode / rt_priv_umode run both trigger modes on the
    S/U-capable ax66_makatau engine paired with QEMU -cpu andes-ax66, with
    CHECK_PRIV asserting the drained privilege on both legs. They execute
    in a new serial phase after the parallel pool: two 32-thread ax66
    processes inside the pool starved the box and timed out unrelated
    tests. The fixtures pad 16 nops after the EXIT marker so the wider
    core's halt slack cannot reach the privilege-changing ecall.

    Suite: 43/43 pass (marker 21, pc 21, neg 1) at JOBS=8.

    Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

